# 1Password env-file for the QA Playwright E2E test-inventory fixture seed
# (GOL-1152). `op run --env-file=.env.op.seed -- python3 seed_e2e_test_inventory.py`
# resolves the op:// references to real values and injects them as the exact
# env vars the seed script reads (ODOO_URL/ODOO_DB/ODOO_USER/ODOO_PASSWORD).
# Consumed by `make qa-l3-seed-e2e`.
#
# Why a SEPARATE env-file from .env.op (blast radius / least privilege):
#   .env.op feeds `terraform apply`; this feeds a data-seed HTTP client. The
#   Odoo admin API key below must never leak into the apply's env, so it lives
#   in its own file scoped to just the seed target. Committed file — it holds
#   op:// references, not secrets (same rationale as .env.op).
#
# Auth account: the resolving `op` account MUST be able to read the `Grove QA`
# vault (grove-devops-ro reads Grove QA + Admin). grove-ci-prod-ro — the
# GitHub-Actions SA behind OP_CI_SA_TOKEN — is read-only to Grove Prod and
# CANNOT read Grove QA, which is why this seed is a LOCAL-OPS make target rather
# than a GitHub Actions job. Provisioning a Grove-QA-scoped CI SA (board-owned)
# is the prerequisite to moving it into CI.
#
# Refs are by item UUID + field id (not name/label) so a rename can't break
# resolution — same convention as .env.op (GOL-394). Item
# fffizd2jrpmkknyeeke5dxnziy = "Gather At the Grove QA Odoo" in vault `Grove QA`.

# Non-secret targeting — plain literals resolved as-is by `op run`.
ODOO_URL="https://odoo.qa.gatheringatthegrove.com"
ODOO_DB="odoo"

# Admin login (uid 2) + its API key, used as XML-RPC (login, password). An Odoo
# user API key authenticates as that user over XML-RPC when passed as password.
ODOO_USER="op://Grove QA/fffizd2jrpmkknyeeke5dxnziy/username"
ODOO_PASSWORD="op://Grove QA/fffizd2jrpmkknyeeke5dxnziy/lnafslr75vidqs7tymuju6bvpa"
